WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:07.856
Forty-four percent of Military Police Complaints Commission recommendations rejected by the Canadian Forces Provost Marshal in 2024.

00:00:07.806 --> 00:00:15.500
Complaints surged three hundred and eighty-three percent — from twelve in 2020-21 to fifty-eight in 2022-24.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:21.715
There is zero military whistleblower protection equivalent to the United States' Title 10 Section 1034.

00:00:21.715 --> 00:00:28.034
Following Lieutenant-Colonel Hiestand's death by suicide, the MPCC issued thirteen recommendations.

00:00:28.034 --> 00:00:30.363
All thirteen were rejected.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:37.499
Major General Dany Fortin's CFNIS investigation was described as compromised by tunnel vision — he was acquitted.

00:00:37.499 --> 00:00:44.579
Lieutenant General Steve Whelan was charged in July 2022; charges were withdrawn in October 2023.

00:00:44.579 --> 00:00:53.909
Active investigations continue under MPCC-2024-047 through MPCC-2024-043.

00:00:53.909 --> 00:00:57.647
The pattern is consistent: investigate, delay, absolve.
